# ncar-hpc-deploy cadences: `ncar-hpc-deploy tick --lane L CADENCE` runs, in file order, every
# row whose cadence, host and lane match. Cron says when a cadence fires (etc/crontab.<lane>);
# this file says what it runs. Ships in the image, so a new step is smoke-tested with its job.
# A failed step does not stop the tick. rapid/hourly skip a step whose job lock is held;
# other cadences wait for it (NCAR_HPC_DEPLOY_STEP_WAIT, 1800 s).
# cadence  hosts           lanes     job [args]
rapid      casper,derecho  prod,dev  collectors
rapid      casper,derecho  prod      jobhist-sync rapid
hourly     casper,derecho  prod,dev  accounting-comp --last 2d
daily      casper,derecho  prod      jobhist-sync daily
daily      casper,derecho  prod,dev  accounting-comp --last 7d
daily      casper          prod,dev  accounting-disk
weekly     casper,derecho  prod      jobhist-sync weekly
